WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.883
Type-C adds variants

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.557
pattern matching generics

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.795
and errors-as-values

00:00:04.607 --> 00:00:05.644
to C11

00:00:06.174 --> 00:00:07.306
Type-C is a

00:00:07.117 --> 00:00:08.756
C11 superset whose

00:00:08.568 --> 00:00:10.053
compiler typec

00:00:10.148 --> 00:00:11.197
translates it to

00:00:11.021 --> 00:00:12.211
readable C and

00:00:12.023 --> 00:00:12.836
hands it to

00:00:12.648 --> 00:00:13.579
your normal C

00:00:13.391 --> 00:00:14.157
compiler

00:00:14.686 --> 00:00:15.617
The author built

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:16.136
it to tame

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:17.669
parsing tree walking

00:00:17.481 --> 00:00:18.636
and error handling

00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:19.344
in C without

00:00:19.155 --> 00:00:20.299
porting to Rust

00:00:20.205 --> 00:00:21.643
Swift or OCaml

00:00:22.166 --> 00:00:23.581
A C11 file

00:00:23.392 --> 00:00:24.182
is already a

00:00:23.994 --> 00:00:25.267
Type-C file so

00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:26.246
a program adopts

00:00:26.057 --> 00:00:26.918
it one file

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:27.508
at a time

00:00:27.647 --> 00:00:28.755
/ Applies a

00:00:28.566 --> 00:00:29.521
line such as

00:00:29.345 --> 00:00:30.500
add 5 or

00:00:30.324 --> 00:00:31.432
neg to total

00:00:31.974 --> 00:00:32.988
Full story on

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:33.695
the dashboard
